een wouldn't start to pick  up steam until the late 90s she appeared  in 10 feature films between 1996 and  2000 when she made her debut on Sex in  the City  Cohen had done TV before but portraying  Cynthia Nixon's Ukrainian made a nanny  on the smash hit HBO show exposed her to  whole new levels of Fame yes she  reprised the role of Magda in the 2008  Sex in the City movie as well as its  2010 sequel several former Sex in the  City cast members took to social media  after hearing about Cohen's passing the  leading lady included Sarah Jessica  Parker wrote on an Instagram post  beautiful Lynn Cohen  dear and necessary Magda our dear SATC  colleague talent race inspiration  r.i.p meanwhile actor Willie Garson  tweeted bless you and Godspeed our  wonderful Magda for 15 years of episodes  and films thank you for your friendship  and amazing talent Hawaii born actress  Kelly nakahara died of cancer in  February 20 21 at her home in California  she was 72 years old nakahara was best  known for her role as nurse Kelly on the  classic Army Hospital drama team Ashe  her sister Nalani Coleman told CNN she  was a performer and an artist and she  did her artwork to make people happy  which in turn gave her joy people wanted  to be near her she was genuine in her  persona nakahara was only supposed to be  an extra on mash but she had different  plans  she once explained I put myself in every  scene and nobody told me to get out and  that tactic worked perfectly  gende enough featuring in 167 episodes  of the korean war set show even playing  the lead on occasion Alan Alda who  portrayed surgeon Hawkeye Pierce told  Fox News she was adorable and brilliant  in the part but you couldn't beat what  she was as a person funnier and warmer  and kinder than most people I've known  actress and musician Sinead Dubois best  known for playing fashionable divorcee  Willona woods on the 70s sitcom good  times passed away in her California home  in February 2020 to her family she was  74 at the time although the New York  Times reported that public records  indicated she may actually have been  older Dubois was born in Philadelphia  but moved to New York to pursue a career  in acting she appeared in several  Broadway productions and ran her own  acting workshop for kids at one stage  but by the 1960s Hollywood was calling  the ambitious performer was cast in good  times in 1974 but trained Willona woods  until 1979 and appearing in a total of a  hundred and thirty three episodes of the  Norman Lear sitcom during her stint on  good times Dubois told Lear that she  wanted to explore new avenues and he  suggested that she create a song for the  Jeffersons one of the prolific producers  many shows the results was movin on up  which according to the New York Times  became one of the era's most iconic  theme songs as well as an empowering  aspirational song for black Americans  Dubois daughter Keisha Gupta Fields  later said it provided a lot of black  people with an anthem the Philly native  went  to appear in a handful of feature films  in the years that followed but she was  always more celebrated for her TV work  dubois also won two Primetime Emmys for  her work on eddie murphy and larry  wilmore's animated series the PJs in  which she voiced the quarrelsome housing  project resident mrs. Avery swedish-born  actor Max von Sydow best known to  American audiences for playing father  Merrin and The Exorcist and Ming the  Merciless in Flash Gordon passed away in  March 2020  he was 90 years old the imposing  european landed on Hollywood's radar  after appearing in a string of movies by  acclaimed Swedish filmmaker Ingmar  Bergman von Sydow initially spurned US  advances but when the chance to play  Jesus Christ and the greatest story ever  told came his way in 1965 he decided to  take his talent stateside The Exorcist  and Flash Gordon further established him  in America though he would go on to be  typecast as a swab evildoer in the years  that followed most notably in 1983 s  never say never again  replay classic Bond villain blow field  in the Sean Connery flick Lance Ito  stayed active late into his career  appearing in a number of big Hollywood  franchises he portrayed Explorer lor San  Tekka in 2015 Star Wars Episode 7 the  force awakens and later appeared in  three episodes of Game of Thrones  playing the all-knowing three-eyed Raven  director Edgar Wright led the tributes  on Twitter calling von Sydow a quote  iconic presence in cinema for seven  decades he is survived by his wife  Katherine and four sons sadly these  aren't the only actors who have left us  in 2020 here are some of the other stars  who enhanced our lives before leaving us  all too soon John shrapnel Esther Scott  Jason Davis Rafael Coleman if you or  anyone you know is having suicidal  thoughts please call the National  Suicide Prevention lifeline at 1-800 to  73 talk eight two five five  [Music]
 

